#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 480.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193425} :activity/id #uuid "157f57f7-71ad-5178-b6a1-cb1065e17520" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050448 :topic/id #uuid "49d2d213-870d-5feb-be49-bffbb6cbe24a" :topic/math-academy-id 4029} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193425 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193943 :tutorial/content "A valuable skill to master when dealing with absolute value equations is to isolate the absolute value expression first.\n\nTo isolate an absolute value expression, we treat it like a variable in a linear equation.\n\nTo demonstrate, let's consider the following absolute value equation:\n\n$$\n2|x-1| + 4 = 8\n$$\n\nWe aim to isolate the $|x-1|$ term on the left-hand side. \n\nWe start by subtracting $4$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2|x-1|+4 & =8 \\\\ 2|x-1|+4-4 & =8-4 \\\\ 2|x-1| & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides of the equation by $2{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2|x-1| & =4 \\\\ \\frac{2|x-1|}{2} & =\\frac{4}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{2}|x-1|}{\\cancel{2}} & =2 \\\\ |x-1| & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAnd that's it! We've successfully isolated the absolute value expression in our equation.\n\nLet's consider another example." :tutorial/id #uuid "640fe647-93cb-5b1a-8707-6c53032d81ae" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8824 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "b4b80cf6-ac66-5b80-8e9a-84e34ac2fd5d" :step/math-academy-id 144049 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193426}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193426 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192634 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192592 :question/id #uuid "b3b99d07-5914-578b-9aaf-f028ada5bee0" :question/math-academy-id "e-14220"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5bc2c576-4f7c-5b4a-8c78-8a41420fdcce" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048267}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193128} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193245} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487339} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487365} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487368}] :knowledge-point/title "Isolating an Absolute Value Expression"} :step/id #uuid "6e54dac3-7257-553a-9281-d652e78869f1" :step/math-academy-id 144050 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193427}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193427 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193944 :tutorial/content "Let's consider the following absolute value equation:\n\n$$\n\\vert x \\vert = -4\n$$\n\nNote the following:\n\n- The absolute value of any number is *always* positive or zero.\n\n- So, there is no number whose absolute value is negative.\n\n- Therefore, this equation $|x| = -4$ has **no solution.**\n\nAnother way of understanding this is to recall that the absolute value of a number represents the number's distance from the origin, and distances cannot be negative." :tutorial/id #uuid "b272858e-f85c-5daa-ad70-c87f7a3b792f" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8826 :tutorial/title "Recognizing Equations With No Solution"} :step/id #uuid "1f7f7690-789e-59b6-a31a-f699646aed1e" :step/math-academy-id 144054 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193428}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193428 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193945 :tutorial/content "So, we know that the following equation has no solution:\n\n$$\n\\vert x \\vert = -4\n$$\n\nLet's see what happens when we blindly apply the usual process of solving our equation:\n\n- if $|x| = x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|x| & =-4 \\\\ x & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- if $|x| = -x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|x| & =-4 \\\\ -x & =-4 \\\\ x & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the usual process has given us the \"solutions\" $x= {\\color{red}{-4}}$ and $x= {\\color{blue}{4}}.$ However, neither of these values satisfies the original equation!\n\nFor example, by substituting $x = {\\color{blue}{4}}$ into the original equation, we get a *false statement!*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|x| & =-4 \\\\ |4| & =-4 \\\\ 4 & =-4\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe key takeaway is that it's essential to check that the right-hand side is positive (or zero) *before* applying the usual solution process." :tutorial/id #uuid "ea3bc553-4605-5ceb-8f0b-e788bb67414a" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8827 :tutorial/title "Attempting to Solve an Equation With No Solution"} :step/id #uuid "dd2c5b77-7fcb-5443-969e-13f565428281" :step/math-academy-id 144055 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193429}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193429 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192635 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192593 :question/id #uuid "89382e45-4e78-554f-88e1-2bbf281617e9" :question/math-academy-id "e-14223"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "94d6a2aa-4288-51dc-8944-cf9490812ad2" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193131} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193370} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487333} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487392}] :knowledge-point/title "Absolute Value Equations With No Solution"} :step/id #uuid "cc568d38-8ed7-5e05-b47d-35fcd03f33e3" :step/math-academy-id 144056 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193430}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193430 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192636 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192594 :question/id #uuid "de2efe4f-e236-5fb2-bc46-eb037ecf26b1" :question/math-academy-id "e-14228"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "15f03573-42ee-50d4-acdf-e2ee05d3e7e4" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193246} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193251} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487342} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487353} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487381} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487385}] :knowledge-point/title "Rearranging and Solving an Absolute Value Equation"} :step/id #uuid "9aebc5c1-cf53-5a78-8700-b622cd65203b" :step/math-academy-id 144059}] :activity/title "Further Absolute Value Equations" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186192907}]}
